@startuml t6c_fuselage_simple

' Simplified overview of t6c_fuselage.hpp/.cpp: the shape of the API plus
' the 1-call sequence. "Your Aero Model" is drawn explicitly as the caller
' so every arrow is an accurate "who calls whom" -- the library's own data
' types (Geometry, TuningParams, Output) never call anything themselves,
' they're just data passed into/out of the one real call.
' Preview in VS Code: open this file, press Alt+D.

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty members

class "Your Aero Model" as YourAero <<caller, outside this library>>

class FuselageModel {
  +FuselageModel(geometry, tuning)
  +Update(state) : Output
}

class Geometry {
  Lf_m, df_m
  Ln_m, Lc_m, Lt_m, db_m
  theta_rad, psi_rad
  Sw_m2, mac_m, b_m
}

class TuningParams {
  windshield_drag_increment
}
class "PitchTuning" as PitchT {
  cm0_fr_slope, dcm0_nose_*, dcm0_tail_*
  cma_fr_slope, dcma_nose_*, dcma_tail_*
  <<anchored at Eq.13/14 -- real paper numbers>>
}
class "YawTuning" as YawT {
  cnb_fr_slope, dcnb_nose_*, dcnb_tail_*
  <<anchored at Eq.16 -- real paper numbers>>
}

class AeroState {
  V_mps, rho_kgm3, mu_pas, mach
  alpha_rad, beta_rad
}

class Output {
  .. drag (Roskam/Kroo, closed-form) ..
  cd_skin_friction, cd_base, cd_upsweep
  cd_fuselage_sfront, cd_fuselage_sw, drag_n
  .. pitch (Nicolosi, anchored) ..
  cm0, cmalpha, cm, pitch_moment_nm
  .. yaw (Nicolosi, anchored) ..
  cnbeta, cn, yaw_moment_nm
}

TuningParams *-- PitchT : pitch
TuningParams *-- YawT : yaw
FuselageModel *-- Geometry
FuselageModel *-- TuningParams
FuselageModel ..> AeroState : reads (per call)
FuselageModel ..> Output : returns (per call)

YourAero --> FuselageModel : "construct once:\nFuselageModel(geometry, tuning)"
YourAero --> FuselageModel : "① Update(state)"
FuselageModel --> YourAero : returns Output

YourAero ..> YourAero : "② add cd_fuselage_sw into total CD\n(same axis as CDgear);\nfold cm/cn into pitch/yaw moment\n-- or keep using t6texan2.xml's own\nCmo/Cmalpha/Cnb until this is CFD-calibrated"

note right of FuselageModel
  Sfront/Swet/FR/FRn/FRt precomputed
  once in the ctor from Geometry --
  Update() never recomputes them, and
  holds no other state between calls.
end note

note bottom of PitchT
  CM0/CMalpha: anchored at the paper's
  own printed reference-fuselage
  numbers (Eq.13/14), slopes are the
  guess part -- see Sec.5-6.
end note

note bottom of Output
  Scalar CD/CM/CN only -- no direction/
  frame resolution. Caller rotates/
  relocates into body axes itself.
end note

@enduml
